  "comment": "DOMINO BUBBLE TILES, the 2-omino family. A 1x2 rectangle with each long side read as two collinear unit edges is a weakly convex equilateral hexagon, angles 90/180/90/90/180/90. Angle word period 3, so the half turn is a symmetry and the family is (2^6 + 2^3)/2 = 36 tiles, 192 corner classes. maxValence 4 is EXACT and not a bound: the smallest angle is 90, and 4x90 = 360. That exponent is why a square-based polyform is cheaper than a triangle-based one, whose 60-degree corners admit valence 6.",
